s/reuters.com,2026:newsml_L4N43T1AX:0/","gurl":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE1UWnJzcTBwRzczY21KeXpqZ1pxWWdLWk9zMUNqQVZCXy1NR3RLTXV5UmdKcURqLUpCU0pYOHd5ZUYzOTg4dzg1Z3NtLVFNR2V3XzJiV2NBOTExbFZkOEJUZXBsS3liLXNlWGpaODFRaVlBMjU3OUJV?oc=5","linkOk":true},{"id":"g1otz70j","cat":"GP","inst":"Brookfield","instType":"해외 GP","asset":"IN","region":"GL","date":"07.27","time":"23:55","ts":"2026-07-27T14:55:19.000Z","source":"이슈투데이","lang":"ko","ko":"네이버, 엔비디아 전략적 투자와 브룩필드 협력으로 AI 인프라 확장","en":"","metric":"뉴스","metricLabel":"핵심 지표","ai":["네이버, 엔비디아 전략적 투자와 브룩필드 협력으로 AI 인프라 확장 이슈투데이"],"body":"네이버, 엔비디아 전략적 투자와 브룩필드 협력으로 AI 인프라 확장 이슈투데이","fetched":false,"url":"https://www.issuetoday.co.kr/news/article.html?no","gurl":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZkFVX3lxTFBCb3JJTmRLa2FHaVZDZEN2d1VaOFY2MzZxZTkxcklNXzByXzZlWEQwSGRPMjQzdVJnaDRUcWs3Y055WkhwSnBjdWNBNVNCMlJESWNKU0R5RXc5aTdzNHdRY29MSGFHUQ?oc=5","linkOk":true},{"id":"g1p3qj7g","cat":"GP","inst":"Brookfield","instType":"해외 GP","asset":"IN","region":"GL","date":"07.27","time":"23:15","ts":"2026-07-27T14:15:00.000Z","source":"khan.co.kr","lang":"en","ko":"USD 10 billion from Nvidia·Brookfield… Naver secures AI investment·infrastructure financing","en":"USD 10 billion from Nvidia·Brookfield… Naver secures AI investment·infrastructure financing","metric":"뉴스","metricLabel":"핵심 지표","ai":["This article was translated by an AI tool.","Feedback Here .","Naver has secured a total of USD 10 billion (approximately 14.7 trillion KRW) in investment and infrastructure financing from Nvidia and Brookfield."],"body":"This article was translated by an AI tool. Feedback Here .\n\nNaver has secured a total of USD 10 billion (approximately 14.7 trillion KRW) in investment and infrastructure financing from Nvidia and Brookfield. It has signed an agreement with Nvidia to jointly build an artificial intelligence (AI) factory and for a strategic investment, and intends to work with global alternative investment firm Brookfield to arrange large-scale computing infrastructure, with a plan to expand its AI factory business beyond Asia to Europe·the Middle East.\n\nOn the 27th, Naver disclosed that it will carry out a USD 1 billion (approximately 1.47 trillion KRW) paid-in capital increase allocated to Nvidia, which is pursuing the joint construction of a global AI factory.\n\nThis move is seen as an effort to get ahead in securing business opportunities in the global AI computing market by entering into a strategic partnership with Nvidia in response to surging demand for global AI infrastructure and by jointly building large-scale global AI factories. In the AI factory business, Naver will lead site acquisition, construction, and operation of data centers, while Nvidia will participate as the supplier of graphics processing units (GPUs).\n\nNaver has laid out a phased infrastructure plan to build 55㎿(megawatts) by the first half of 2027, 100㎿ by the end of 2027, and 200㎿ by 2028. Naver also presented a goal of generating revenue from the AI factory business starting in 2027.\n\nThe first hub will be the Naver hyperscaler data center ‘Gak Sejong’, after which it plans to expand across the globe beyond the Asia·Pacific to Europe and the Middle East.\n\nNaver also plans to conduct a USD 1 billion third-party allotment paid-in capital increase, issuing 7,241,564 new common shares to Nvidia at 204,500 KRW per share. It is the first time in 22 years that Naver has undertaken a third-party allotment paid-in capital increase, and the first since its transfer listing to KOSPI in 2008.\n\nIn addition, a plan has been proposed under which Brookfield will arrange USD 9 billion (approximately 13.1625 trillion KRW) in computing infrastructure needed to build the AI factory. Brookfield is a frontier investor in AI infrastructure such as data centers and renewable energy.","fetched":true,"url":"https://www.khan.co.kr/en/article/202607272315027","gurl":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE14Y1Vh